<title>SWITZERLAND: FIGURE SKATING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>FIGURE SKATING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the</p>
<p>men's qualifying round at the World figure skating championships</p>
<p>on Sunday (top 15 from each group go through to the main event</p>
<p>beginning on Wednesday):</p>
<p>Group A:</p>
<p>1. Todd Eldredge (U.S.) 1.0 factored placements</p>
<p>2. Elvis Stojko (Canada) 2.0</p>
<p>3. Viacheslav Zagorodniuk (Ukraine) 3.0</p>
<p>4. Andrei Vlascenko (Germany) 4.0</p>
<p>5. Igor Pashkevitch (Azerbaijan) 5.0</p>
<p>6. Alexei Yagudin (Russia) 6.0</p>
<p>7. Szabolcz Vidrai (Hungary) 7.0</p>
<p>8. Cornel Gheorghe (Romania) 8.0</p>
<p>9. Anthony Liu (Australia) 9.0</p>
<p>10. Patrick Schmidt (Luxembourg) 10.0</p>
<p>11. Michael Shmerkin (Israel) 11.0</p>
<p>12. Zhengxin Guo (China) 12.0</p>
<p>13. Ivan Dinev (Bulgaria) 13.0</p>
<p>14. Markus Leminen (Finland) 14.0</p>
<p>15. Vakhtang Murvanidze (Georgia) 15.0</p>
<p>16. Patrick Meier (Switzerland) 16.0</p>
<p>Did not qualify:</p>
<p>17. Alexandre Mourashko (Belarus) 17.0</p>
<p>18. Karel Nekola (Czech Republic) 18.0</p>
<p>19. Ferdi Skoberla (South Africa) 19.0</p>
<p>20. Youri Litvinov (Kazakhstan) 20.0</p>
<p>21. Ricardo Olavarrieta (Mexico) 21.0</p>
<p>22. Yan-Ho Brian Chan (Hong Kong) 22.0</p>
<p>Meier in 16th place qualified to fulfil an ISU requirement</p>
<p>that the host nation have a skater in the main event.</p>
<p>Group B:</p>
<p>1.  Alexei Urmanov (Russia) 1.0</p>
<p>2.  Ilya Kulik (Russia) 2.0</p>
<p>3.  Eric Millot (France) 3.0</p>
<p>4.  Michael Weiss (U.S.) 4.0</p>
<p>5.  Jeff Langdon (Canada) 5.0</p>
<p>6.  Laurent Tobel (France) 6.0</p>
<p>7.  Takeshi Honda (Japan) 7.0</p>
<p>8.  Konstantin Kostin (Latvia) 8.0</p>
<p>9.  Steven Cousins (Britain) 9.0</p>
<p>10. Michael Hopfes (Germany) 10.0</p>
<p>11. Lee Kyu-hyun (South Korea) 11.0</p>
<p>12. Michael Tyllesen (Denmark) 12.0</p>
<p>13. Roman Skorniakov (Uzbekistan) 13.0</p>
<p>14. Gilberto Viadana (Italy) 14.0</p>
<p>15. Robert Grzegorczyk (Poland) 15.0</p>
<p>Did not qualify</p>
<p>16. Jordi Pedro (Spain) 16.0</p>
<p>17. Margus Hernits (Estonia) 17.0</p>
<p>18. Dan Hollander (U.S.) 18.0</p>
<p>19. Robert Kazimir (Slovakia) 19.0</p>
<p>20. David Liu (Taiwan) 20.0</p>
<p>21. Florian Tuma (Austria) 21.0</p>
<p>22. Matthew Van den Broeck (Belgium) 22.0</p>
<p>Withdrew: Armen Asoyan (Armenia)</p>
